# Provider Gate Status

Use this rule when editing checked-in provider gate data, rollup logic, or the
`/provider-status` HTTP response.

## Authoritative Source And Docs Sync

- Canonical gate data is `packages/domain/data/provider-gates.yaml`. Domain
  code loads it via `import.meta.url` relative to
  `packages/domain/src/provider-gates.ts`.
- When YAML changes, keep `docs/01-provider-matrix.md` aligned so humans see
  the same columns as the file.

## YAML Shape And Validation

- `GATE_DIMENSIONS` in `provider-gates.ts` is the single list of required gate
  keys. Each provider `gates` object must include **every** dimension:
  `credentials_tested`, `terms_allow_use_case`, `rate_limits_known`,
  `cost_billing_documented`.
- Each dimension value must be exactly one of: `pending`, `approved`,
  `rejected`, `not_applicable`.

## Task 0.4 Versus Gate Columns

- `task_0_4_external_validation.complete` is a separate boolean in the YAML.
  Do not treat "all gates cleared" (`rollupProviderGateStatus` returns
  `cleared`) as proof that Task 0.4 is done. Set `complete` to `true` only after
  external credential and commercial validation evidence exists.

## Rollup And Actionable

- Per-provider rollup (`rollupProviderGateStatus`): if any gate is `rejected`,
  status is `rejected-gate`. Else if any gate is `pending`, status is
  `pending-gate`. Otherwise status is `cleared`. So `rejected` wins over
  `pending`, and `pending` wins over cleared states (`approved` /
  `not_applicable`).
- `actionable` on the payload is `true` when **any** provider has rollup
  `pending-gate` or `rejected-gate` (`providerGatesActionable` /
  `gatesRequireAction`).

## Provider Identity

- Duplicate `providers[].id` values are invalid. Validation rejects duplicates
  case-insensitively (normalized with `toLowerCase()`).

## Integration Points

- `packages/domain/src/provider-gates.ts`: parse, validate, rollup, and
  `buildProviderStatusPayload` / `getProviderStatusPayload`.
- `packages/domain/src/provider-gates.test.ts`: contracts for YAML loading,
  rollup, uniqueness, and payload shape.
- `apps/service/src/http/provider-status.ts`: Hono handler returning JSON from
  `getProviderStatusPayload()`.

## Pitfalls

- Omitting a `GATE_DIMENSIONS` key under `gates` fails validation even if the
  YAML parses.
- Confusing `actionable` with Task 0.4 completion: the API exposes both; they
  are independent.
- Adding a new gate dimension requires updating `GATE_DIMENSIONS`, the YAML,
  tests, and `docs/01-provider-matrix.md` together.

## Reference Implementation

- Treat `rollupProviderGateStatus`, `providerGatesActionable`, and
  `buildProviderStatusPayload` in `packages/domain/src/provider-gates.ts` as the
  normative definitions for rollup and HTTP payload fields.
